→“A function in JavaScript is a reusable block of code that performs a specific task. It allows us to organize and reuse logic instead of writing the same code multiple times.”
🔹 2. Explain Why We Use Functions
“Functions help in making code modular, reusable, readable, and easier to maintain. Instead of repeating logic, we define it once and call it whenever needed.”
Example:
function add(a, b) {
  return a + b;
}
console.log(add(3, 5)); // Output: 8


🔹 3. Talk About Function Types
You can mention a few main types depending on your comfort level:
✅ Function Declaration
    function sayHi() {
    console.log("Hi!");
    }
    sayHi();

✅ Function Expression
const sayHi = function() {
  console.log("Hi!");
};
sayHi();

✅ Arrow Function (ES6)
const sayHi = () => console.log("Hi!");
sayHi();

✅ Anonymous Function
“A function without a name, often used as a callback.”
setTimeout(function() {
  console.log("Executed after 2 seconds");
}, 2000);


🔹 4. Explain Parameters and Return Values
“Functions can accept inputs called parameters and return output using the return statement.”
function multiply(x, y) {
  return x * y;
}
console.log(multiply(4, 5)); // Output: 20


🔹 5. Explain Scope and Closures (If Asked in Deep Topics)
“Functions create their own scope. Variables declared inside a function are not accessible outside it.”
function test() {
  let message = "Hello";
  console.log(message); // Accessible
}
console.log(message); // ❌ Error: message is not defined

“Also, if a function remembers variables from its parent scope, that’s called a closure.”


